course: dictionary
lesson: 7828
title: One word, three jobs: quiz
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quiz can be a noun or a verb, so the sentence tells you which job it is doing. A quiz can be a short test with questions: «Can or not?» asked Mum, and he did the quiz at home. Here quiz is a thing you do, a test.
explain: A quiz can also be a game where people or teams answer questions to win points. Grandad shouts the questions from the kitchen, everybody grabs a pencil, and every answer can be checked. Look for words like points, teams and winning to show you the game meaning.
explain: Quiz can also be a verb, meaning to ask someone many questions. Read the clue words: if someone is asking, the word is probably a verb. Try the swap check: put «asked many questions» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A quiz is a short test with questions.
fact: A quiz is also a game where people or teams answer questions to win points.
fact: To quiz someone is to ask them many questions. Quizzes and quizzing are forms of the verb.
fact: A pop quiz is a surprise test.
fact: In a maths quiz, points can be worked out as right answers × points for each question. Sometimes wrong answers take points away.
exercise: «Can or not?» asked Mum — Singapore talk for «yes or no?» — and he did the quiz at home. In this sentence, what is a quiz? | *A short test with questions | A walk around the garden | A loud shout | A kind of hot drink
exercise: Grandad shouts the questions from the kitchen, and everybody grabs a pencil. What kind of quiz is this? | A pop quiz on a sports field | A quiz show on TV | A spelling quiz at school | *A family quiz night
exercise: Mum quizzed me on my times tables all evening. What does quizzed mean? | Turned off the lights | Wrote a letter to my teacher | Gave me a present | *Asked me lots of questions
test: A maths quiz gives 5 points for each right answer. If you get 6 right, how many points do you score? | 11 | 56 | *30 | 20
test: Which phrase means a surprise test? | a quiz on fractions | a quiz night | *a pop quiz | a quiz show
exam: Which sentence uses quiz as a verb, meaning to ask many questions? | *Mum quizzed him about the planets all evening | We went to quiz night at school | She won the quiz show prize | The class quiz was on Friday
